##  Job System

As of March 18, 2026, there is currently one available job in the game. Additional jobs will be added as development continues.
The Job System allows the player to earn money while balancing time, stress, and daily responsibilities.
Jobs are a primary source of income but come with trade-offs that directly impact the player’s physical and mental state.

---

##  Core Job Loop

Travel to job → Interact with work terminal → Select shift →  
Time advances → Earn money → Gain stress → Return to world

---

##  Time & Trade-Off Design

Each job forces the player to make decisions between:

-  **Income** — More hours = more money  
-  **Stress** — Longer shifts increase stress  
-  **Time** — Working reduces time available for other activities  

This creates a constant tension between survival and wellbeing.

---

##  Current Job

### Clothing Store (Implemented)

The player can interact with the cash register to open the Work Menu and select a shift.

Each shift:
- Advances in-game time  
- Rewards the player with money  
- Increases stress  

| Work Type | Time Worked | Money Earned | Stress Gained |
|----------|------------|-------------|--------------|
| Part-Time | 4 hours | $40 | +5 |
| Full Time | 8 hours | $80 | +10 |
| Overtime | 12 hours | $120 | +20 |

---

##  World Integration

Jobs are tied to physical locations in the city.

This creates:
- Travel requirements  
- Risk of encountering events (roadblocks, protests)  
- Potential delays or missed work opportunities  

---

##  Dynamic Job Conditions (Future System)

As the city falls into dissent, jobs may be affected by:

- Business closures  
- Reduced hours  
- Increased demand for work  
- Dangerous travel conditions  

This ensures the job system evolves with the world.

---

##  Planned Jobs

Additional jobs will introduce new gameplay variations:

- Personal Trainer (Gym)
  - Reduces stress while earning money  
  - Requires sufficient stamina/morale  

- Cashier (Corner Store)
  - Stable income  
  - Lower stress, lower pay  

- Factory 
  - Higher income but in another district
  - Higher stress gain 

- TV news studio
  - Stable income
  - Medium stress, and lower pay

Future jobs will be distributed across districts to encourage exploration and strategic planning.

---

##  System Interactions

The Job System directly affects:

- Stress → increases with longer shifts  
- Morale → may decrease if overworked  
- Grandpa → less time available for care  
- Time → limits daily actions  
- Economy → enables survival through income  

---

##  Design Purpose

The Job System reinforces the core gameplay loop by forcing the player to constantly make trade-offs.

Players must decide how to allocate their time between:

- Earning money  
- Maintaining their wellbeing  
- Caring for Grandpa  
- Navigating a city in decline  

No choice is optimal—every decision has consequences.
